@page "/ai-assistants"

<DocsHeader Title="AI assistants" Eyebrow="Get started"
            Description="Let Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, Cursor and other assistants write code with Stil's real components, parameters and classes, through the Stil MCP server or the docs as Markdown." />

<p>
    An assistant that has never seen Stil guesses: it writes Bootstrap classes, or parameters a component does not
    have. There are two ways to give it the real thing. The <a href="ai-assistants#mcp">MCP server</a> answers its
    questions about Stil while it works, and the <a href="ai-assistants#markdown">docs as Markdown</a> work with any
    assistant that can read a web page.
</p>

<h2 id="mcp">The MCP server</h2>
<p>
    <code>Stil.Mcp</code> is a <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/">Model Context Protocol</a> server, new in
    Stil 1.3. Assistants that support MCP ask it which components there are, what parameters they take and which
    classes and tokens exist, and look up the examples on this site. Its answers come from the same sources as these
    docs: the libraries, their XML documentation, the docs pages and examples, and the built CSS, so they match the
    version you run.
</p>
<p>
    The server runs locally and talks to the assistant over stdio. It reads nothing from your project, sends nothing
    anywhere and changes no files. There is nothing to install but the .NET 10 SDK: the assistant starts it with
    <code>dnx</code>, which fetches the package from nuget.org the first time. Write <code>Stil.Mcp@@1.3.0</code>
    instead of <code>Stil.Mcp</code> to pin a version.
</p>
<StilAlert Variant="StilVariant.Info" Subtle Title="On a work computer">
    The assistant starts the server as a new program on your computer. Security software on a managed computer may
    not allow that, so check with your IT department first. The <a href="ai-assistants#markdown">docs as Markdown</a>
    need nothing to run.
</StilAlert>

<h3 id="claude-code">Claude Code</h3>
<CodeBlock Language="shell" Code="claude mcp add stil -- dnx Stil.Mcp --yes" />

<h3 id="vs-code">VS Code</h3>
<p>For GitHub Copilot, add the server to <code>.vscode/mcp.json</code> in your project:</p>
<CodeBlock Language="json" Code="@VsCodeSnippet" />

<h3 id="visual-studio">Visual Studio</h3>
<p>Put the same content in <code>.mcp.json</code> next to the solution.</p>

<h3 id="cursor">Cursor</h3>
<p>Add the server to <code>.cursor/mcp.json</code>:</p>
<CodeBlock Language="json" Code="@CursorSnippet" />

<h3 id="tools">What it can answer</h3>
<p>
    Every tool only reads. When an assistant connects, the server also asks it to use Stil components and
    <code>stil-*</code> classes, and to look a component up before it uses one.
</p>
<div class="stil-table-responsive">
    <table class="stil-table stil-table-compact">
        <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it answers</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var (tool, answer) in Tools)
            {
                <tr><th scope="row"><code class="docs-type">@tool</code></th><td>@answer</td></tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h2 id="markdown">The docs as Markdown</h2>
<p>
    Every page on this site also has a Markdown copy without the menus and previews, at its address with
    <code>.md</code> added (<code>components/buttons.md</code>, and <code>index.html.md</code> for the home page).
    Two files list them, following the <a href="https://llmstxt.org/">llms.txt</a> convention:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>llms.txt</code>: a short introduction and a link to every page, with what it covers. Give an assistant this one, and it can read the pages it needs.</li>
    <li><code>llms-full.txt</code>: every page in one file, for an assistant that should have all of it at once.</li>
</ul>
<CodeBlock Language="text" Code="@MarkdownSnippet" />

<h2 id="tips">Tips</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Say which library to use.</strong> "Build the orders page with Stil components" works better than "build the orders page", even with the server connected.</li>
    <li><strong>Start a new app from the template.</strong> The server's <code>new_project</code> tool gives the same <code>dotnet new</code> command as the <a href="new-app">New app</a> page, so the assistant starts from a project that is already set up.</li>
    <li><strong>Check what it built.</strong> The build tells you about a parameter that does not exist; a CSS class that does not exist only shows on the page.</li>
</ul>

@code {
    private static readonly (string Tool, string Answer)[] Tools =
    [
        ("list_components", "Every component, grouped by docs page, optionally for one package."),
        ("get_component", "A component's package, namespace, parameters, enum values, docs page and examples."),
        ("get_type", "An enum's values, or the members of an option, model or service."),
        ("search", "Components, types, docs pages, CSS classes and tokens that match a word."),
        ("list_css_classes", "The class families, or every class with a prefix such as stil-btn."),
        ("list_tokens", "The --stil-* tokens and their defaults."),
        ("get_example", "An example's Razor source from this site, or the examples of a component."),
        ("new_project", "The dotnet new stil-app or stil-site command for a starter and features."),
        ("add_to_existing_app", "The package, Program.cs, App.razor and layout setup of an existing app."),
    ];

    private const string VsCodeSnippet = """
        {
          "servers": {
            "stil": {
              "type": "stdio",
              "command": "dnx",
              "args": ["Stil.Mcp", "--yes"]
            }
          }
        }
        """;

    private const string CursorSnippet = """
        {
          "mcpServers": {
            "stil": {
              "command": "dnx",
              "args": ["Stil.Mcp", "--yes"]
            }
          }
        }
        """;

    private const string MarkdownSnippet = """
        https://dradwul.github.io/Stil/llms.txt
        https://dradwul.github.io/Stil/llms-full.txt
        """;
}
